'''Tanjiro Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be obtained when beating any stage in [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event#Demon Slayer Corps Final Selection|Demon Slayer Corps Final Selection]] during the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 15.1 Update#Version 15.1.1 Update|Version 15.1.1]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 848
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Tanjiro Cat
|name2 = Tanjiro Cat CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tanjiro Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Tanjiro Cat is such a pathetic excuse of a crowd-controller that it's almost sad, really. His 2.5 second [[Slow]] doesn't even cover his own 4.63 second attack rate, even if you count [[Blood Fruit]] which increases the Slow duration to 3 seconds. But on top of that, he only has a 50% chance to even land a Slow on an enemy in the first place.

Then there's his range. He gets outranged by even a basic peon like [[Sir Seal]]. That's all that needs to be said. The only notable things he has over pre-[[True Form]] [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] are Area Attack and Health, as well as lower cost, but Witch Cat's True Form covers the health problem, and Area Attack doesn't matter when his only viable targets are [[Bore]], [[One Horn]] and [[Red Cyclone]]. His mediocre health and god-awful DPS combined with his 7.87-second recharge make even his use in [[Underground Labyrinth]] questionable.

{{Job|Classification = User Rank Dump & Crowd-Controller}}

